## Repos available

Use these existing local clones — do NOT clone new copies. Edit the list to
match your machine before running the daemon.

- ~/Workspace/your-repo
- ~/Workspace/another-repo

## How to work on code

Create a git worktree alongside the source repo (NOT inside `{{ workspace_path }}`),
for example:

    git -C ~/Workspace/your-repo worktree add \
        ~/Workspace/your-repo-worktrees/{{ issue.identifier | downcase }} \
        -b stevedore/{{ issue.identifier | downcase }}

Do all editing, building, and testing inside that worktree. The scratch dir
above is just for ticket-level notes and intermediate files.

You own branch hygiene: clean up the branch and run `git worktree prune` in
each source repo before you finish.

When the task is complete, remove the `{{ gate_label }}` label from the
ticket via your Jira tool (acli or MCP) so the daemon stops considering it.
